  "limits": "Prefix witnesses are dense in shared Cell instruction order. Scalars and terminal/suffix atoms have no retained witness slots. The existing branching flag is replaced by the required witness width, which also bounds scratch capacity. Projection uses those same static instructions; no runtime source map or reverse dependencies are added. Recursive failure/error/budget exits unwind the witness stack. Leases, visibility, epochs, invalidation and all matched table witnesses remain. Copied-slot counts are not allocation calls or a time model; push/pop and static projection traversal are not separately instruction-counted. Full query/cache integration and speed acceptance remain pending.",
